# (auto-translated)
#: ../hacks/config/kallisti.xml.h:18
msgid ""
"\n"
"The golden apple of discord.\n"
"\n"
"Greek goddess Eris was not invited to a wedding; her retort was to toss in "
"a\n"
"golden apple, inscribed: \"to the fairest\".  Hera, Athena and Aphrodite\n"
"squabbled over it; Zeus noped out, telling Paris of Troy to decide. They "
"all\n"
"cheated, but Aphrodite won by letting Paris abduct and marry Helen of "
"Sparta.\n"
"The Greeks objected to this, leading to the Trojan War.\n"
"\n"
"Do you want to launch a thousand ships? Because this is how you launch a\n"
"thousand ships.\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judgement_of_Paris\n"
"\n"
"Written by Jamie Zawinski and Jared Williams; 2024.\n"
"  "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Spenningens gyldne eple.\n"
"\n"
"Den greske gudinnen Eris ble ikke invitert til et bryllup; replikken hennes "
"var å kaste inn en\n"
"gulleple, påskrevet: \"til de vakreste\".  Hera, Athena og Afrodite\n"
"kranglet om det; Zevs sluttet og ba Paris av Troja bestemme seg. De alle "
"sammen\n"
"jukset, men Afrodite vant ved å la Paris bortføre og gifte seg med Helen av "
"Sparta.\n"
"Grekerne protesterte mot dette, noe som førte til den trojanske krigen.\n"
"\n"
"tusen skip.Vil du sjøsette tusen skip? For det er slik du starter en\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judgement_of_Paris\n"
"\n"
"Skrevet av Jamie Zawinski og Jared Williams; 2024.\n"
"  "

